### "never commit these mistakes" to github ###
# .venv/
# .env 
# .venv/ is a local virtual environment folder, and .env is a local environment variable file. Both of these files should never be committed to GitHub, as they contain sensitive information and are specific to your local development environment.

putting .venv/ and .env in the .gitignore file ensures that they are not tracked by Git, preventing accidental commits of sensitive data. This is a best practice for maintaining security and privacy in your projects.